-- §11  Whether a fused supply still arrives in whole units, and where that question has no answer.
# One row per composed layer every one of whose parts is lumpy: the greatest common divisor of the
# parts' quanta, each converted into the composed layer's unit, and a typed absence where there is
# none.
#
# Every attainable sum is a multiple of the gcd
#   Each part's nameplate is a whole number of its own quanta, so every sum the parts could make is
#   a multiple of the gcd and no larger quantum divides them all. Not every multiple is attainable,
#   because nobody holds a negative number of units: `q = 4` and `q = 6` never make 2. Proof:
#   `src/proofs/README.md`, entry `composed_quantum`.
#
# Two absences, two facts
#   `unmeasured` where a part's conversion factor is: nobody sized it, so nobody can say what the
#   parts share. `notApplicable` where the converted quanta still sit in different units, which is
#   a question that is malformed rather than unanswered.
#
# `1` is a real answer
#   Not a failure. Every integer is a multiple of one, so the constraint is vacuous and the fused
#   supply is continuous as far as the arithmetic can see.
-- composition/composed_quantum.sqlc, ordered by whether the question has an answer.
SELECT c.composition                                   AS "composition!",
       c.composed_layer                                AS "composed_layer!",
       c.parts                                         AS "parts!",
       coalesce(c.unit, '(none)')                      AS "unit!",
       coalesce(c.composed_quantum::text || CASE WHEN c.spread THEN ' (at a factor''s mode)' ELSE '' END,
                '(' || c.absent || ')')                AS "quantum!"
FROM (
    :compose(composition/composed_quantum.sqlc)
) c
ORDER BY (c.absent IS NOT NULL) DESC, c.composition, c.composed_layer
